<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Assertion&nbsp;(A):</strong></td><td style="text-align: justify;">When height of a tube is less than liquid rise in the capillary tube, the liquid does not overflow.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reason&nbsp;(R):</strong></td><td style="text-align: justify;">Product of radius of meniscus and height of liquid in capillary tube always remains constant.</td></tr></tbody></table>
